123:{"timestamp":"2026-07-23T05:11:48.055Z","type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"agent_message","message":"The universal proof now closes with `#Top`. I found and fixed the substantive claim-framing issue as well: loading the module intentionally leaves the `modp` closure in module scope, so the destination configuration must record that state change. I’m doing a final cleanup so the claim names the mathematical contract directly, then I’ll capture the reproducible commands in `prove.sh` and rerun it end-to-end.","phase":"commentary","memory_citation":null}}
